.DS_Store
*.log
*.py[cod]
.venv/
__pycache__/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.coverage
.coverage.*
htmlcov/
build/
dist/
*.egg-info/

# Credentials belong outside the repository. Example files are safe to track.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Agents work in their own worktree under here. They are checkouts, not
# content: a `git add -A` in the main checkout would otherwise commit every
# other agent's working copy into the tree.
.claude/worktrees/

# Machine-local permissions and the quarantine paths. `autoclave/README.md` says
# this file "is gitignored and machine-local, which is the right home for a path" —
# and a review found that nothing in this repository made that true. The only thing
# ignoring it was `~/.config/git/ignore`, a user-level file no clone carries, so on
# any other machine it was an ordinary untracked file holding absolute paths to the
# quarantined old code and a list of pre-approved commands. That is the same failure
# CLAUDE.md devotes a section to for git hooks: a setting outside the repository
# never travels with a clone. One line here makes the claim true everywhere.
.claude/settings.local.json

# Local working areas. The README in each explains the rule and is versioned;
# the contents never are.
workbench/*
!workbench/README.md

# workbench/active/ was tracked briefly, to see what a reviewer would make of the
# run plan. The answer was worth having: CodeRabbit read RUN_PLAN.md and
# independently found a picker instruction in it, which GOVERNANCE 3 forbids
# outright — a defect in the plan propagates into everything built afterwards,
# and nobody reading the code would ever have found it.
#
# It is ignored again because these are task files with a lifecycle, not records.
# `session-end` files them into archive/ when the work closes, so tracking them
# meant tracking things whose whole purpose is to move: added in one session's
# diff and deleted in the next. The history of this branch keeps what was there.
private/*
!private/README.md
scriptorium/*
!scriptorium/README.md

# autoclave/ is deliberately NOT ignored: drafts commit there on work branches
# so the reviewers can read them raw. CI refuses to merge until it is empty,
# which is what keeps main sterile — see autoclave/README.md.
